; DEFAULT: the default graphics set, &F34 bytes loaded at &4000, as the
; Graphics Designer saves it. The designer loads it at &4000 when it starts,
; edits it there and saves &4000-&4F33 back; MISSION loads a graphics file
; like it to put in a mission, and IO carries the same pictures and names.
; The pictures are numbered as slots, &00-&28 (sprites.6502inc says what
; each slot is for); the set itself, every picture drawn, is
; src/default.6502inc.
;
;   &000  slots &00-&27, the graphics: the large sprites &00-&0F (16 x 32
;         pixels, &80 bytes each), the small &10-&1F (8 x 16, &20 bytes),
;         the large &20-&27
;   &E00  what MISSION calls the names: slot &28, then the names of the
;         objects whose icons are small slots &10-&1E, 12 characters each
;
; The designer's sprite sheet (its grid of every picture) shows the large
; slots in its own order: slot_of_position in src/hidden_graphic.6502.
INCLUDE "sprites.6502inc"
INCLUDE "default.6502inc"

SECTION default, filename="DEFAULT", org=SET_LOAD_ADDRESS, load=SET_LOAD_ADDRESS, exec=&0

.graphics
    EQUB default_graphics()
.names
    ASSERT names - graphics = SET_NAMES - LARGE_SPRITE_SIZE
    EQUB default_names()
    ASSERT P% - graphics = SET_SIZE

ENDSECTION
